# Variant of 332f06d7
# Dimension: D12 — 通道拓扑：分支与环路 (path)
# Change: 通道为单一蜿蜒路径，无分支无环路，从起点到终点只有一条路... → 管道网络

"""
Design analysis for the D12 variant
===================================

spec_variant:
  preserved_core:
    grid: square 11-20
    colors:
      background: 3
      river: 1
      mover: 0
      destination: 2
    objects:
      mover: solid n x n black square
      destination: solid n x n red square
      channel_pixels: blue
    motion_rule:
      - The mover still slides by testing feasible n x n top-left placements.
      - A placement is feasible iff the whole n x n window lies inside {river,mover,destination}.
      - If the destination placement is reachable, mover covers destination.
      - Otherwise it stops at the farthest reachable feasible placement.

  d12_change_concretized:
    old_visual:
      - Blue river was a single corridor: every feasible placement lay on one chain.
      - A stuck case was just one narrow gate on that chain.
    new_visual:
      - The blue region is a small pipe network with at least one branch node and one loop.
      - The mover starts near one border; destination still touches a border.
      - In reachable cases, the destination is somewhere inside the same network component.
      - In stuck cases, the network is still present, but the final tail to the destination passes
        through a narrowed edge whose width is < n, so the mover explores the network but cannot
        enter the destination tail.

  concrete_behavior_trace:
    example:
      - Suppose n=2 and the feasible-placement graph has a trunk, a side branch, and a 4-cycle.
      - Original task: BFS from mover walks along one line, so "farthest reachable" is just the
        last point before the choke.
      - Variant: BFS now explores a graph. It may enter a loop, back out, and continue along a
        different branch toward the destination.
      - Stuck variant: the choke is placed only on the final tail after the loop/branch area, so
        the mover must reason over a true network first, then stop at the unique last placement
        before the narrowed tail.

  complexity_calibration:
    kept_small_on_purpose:
      - Only four colors, unchanged from the original task.
      - Only two network templates are used: a richer 5x5 coarse template and a compact 4x4 one.
      - Templates are varied by rotation / mirror, so the visual rule is stable but not fixed to
        one orientation.
    why_not_larger:
      - If too many branch types / symbols were added, samples would become noisy.
      - If the graph were fully random, generation would be brittle and visual regularity would
        suffer.
      - Restricting n to 2..3 is a deliberate adaptation: with n=4 and a max 20x20 grid there is
        not enough room to keep non-adjacent branches visually separated by background gaps, and
        with n=1 the topology becomes much less visually diagnostic because narrow gates disappear.

  implicit_assumption_audit_for_main:
    - Background-from-corners still holds because generation keeps all four corners color 3.
    - Solid-square detection still holds because mover/destination remain monochromatic n x n
      squares and no other non-bg component forms a solid square of the same size.
    - River-color detection as the most common remaining non-bg color still holds because the
      network is still entirely blue and occupies more area than either square.
    - The crucial old assumption that "the channel is a single path" is not actually hardcoded in
      BFS; the solver already runs on the whole feasible-placement mask. Therefore main() only needs
      to stay graph-generic, not corridor-specific.
    - The old row-major tie-break for farthest reachable positions would be fragile on a graph if
      many maxima existed. The generator avoids depending on that incidental detail by making the
      reachable component's farthest placement unique in stuck cases.

  placement_legality:
    - A coarse template is rendered into pixel space using anchor offsets separated by at least
      n+1 pixels, so two coarse nodes that are adjacent in the template only connect when an edge
      is explicitly painted.
    - Destination is extended straight to a border only through cells that are still background or
      river, so extension never overwrites the mover or creates ambiguous overlaps.
    - The choke is placed on the final tail edge only; no alternate loop bypasses it.

  visual_observability:
    - Every accepted sample must have at least one degree>=3 node and at least one cycle in the
      mover-reachable feasible-placement component.
    - This metric is computed from the same feasible n x n placement graph that main() uses, so the
      topology is not merely decorative at pixel level; it affects the actual motion space.

  visual_cleanliness:
    - No extra markers are introduced.
    - Branches and loops are separated by background gaps unless intentionally connected.
    - Only one layer of geometry exists: blue pipe, black mover, red destination, green background.

  new_main_assumptions_and_generator_guarantees:
    - main() assumes the mover's own placement is feasible. generate_input() checks that.
    - main() assumes exactly one river color besides the two square colors. generation preserves it.
    - main() is allowed to keep its generic farthest-placement fallback because the generator makes
      stuck-case maxima unique and validates the full output against main(grid).
